* [ ] Job completion notifications
* [ ] Command aliases
* [ ] More shell builtins
* [ ] Automated tests
* [ ] Improved POSIX compatibility

## Why Cpell?

The goal of Cpell isn't simply to create another command-line interface.

It is a hands-on project for understanding what happens underneath a Unix shell:

```text
             Cpell
               |
       +-------+-------+
       |       |       |
     fork()  signals  parser
       |
   process group
       |
   terminal control
       |
    execvp()
       |
 external program
       |
   waitpid()
```

Building these components from scratch makes it possible to understand the relationship between a shell, processes, the terminal, and the Linux kernel.

